IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-fixtures`
IMPORT `ucta-schedules`
IMPORT `ucta-p1-introductory`

-- Tests for ucta-p1-introductory.l4 (section 1).  Every expected value is written from the text.
-- `mk scope` takes: the liability is business liability; kind of contract; what the contract relates to;
-- goods carried by ship or hovercraft; the contract specifies that means over part of the journey;
-- the contract makes no provision and does not exclude it; the term operates for the carriage;
-- the person protected deals as consumer; the person protected is the employee.

§ `s 1(1) - negligence`

#ASSERT `s 1(1) the breach is negligence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the breach is negligence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the breach is negligence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither (a) nor (b): "negligence means ..." is a definition, so a stricter duty is not negligence.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the breach is negligence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 1(3) - business liability`

#ASSERT `s 1(3) the liability is business liability` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the liability is business liability` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 1(4) - inadvertent or intentional, direct or vicarious`

#ASSERT `s 1(4) it makes a difference for this Part` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) it makes a difference for this Part` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 1(2) and (3) - whether an exception takes the section out of the case`

-- Business liability, no Schedule matter, no Part 3 exception: no exception for Section 2(1).
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(1)` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(2)` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 4` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 5` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 6` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 7` (`an ordinary scope`) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`

-- s 1(3): sections 2 to 7 apply "only to business liability".
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(1)` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(2)` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 4` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 5` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 7` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- A non-business liability under a contract that is neither a sale nor hire-purchase is out of section 6.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 6` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 6` (`mk scope` FALSE `A contract, not of sale of goods or hire-purchase, under which possession or ownership of goods passes` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
-- s 6(4): section 6 includes liabilities arising under any contract of sale of goods or hire-purchase agreement.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 6` (`mk scope` FALSE `A contract of sale of goods` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 6` (`mk scope` FALSE `A hire-purchase agreement` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`
-- s 6(4) is within section 6 only: section 7, 2 and 5 stay limited to business liability.
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 7` (`mk scope` FALSE `A contract of sale of goods` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 5` (`mk scope` FALSE `A contract of sale of goods` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
#ASSERT `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(2)` (`mk scope` FALSE `A hire-purchase agreement` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`

